 # Changelog
 
+## 0.2.11 (unreleased)
+
+- New (issue #719): `FfmpegCommand::h264_compatible_input()` and `h264_compatible_input_with(filters)`
+  add `-vf pad=ceil(iw/2)*2:ceil(ih/2)*2 -pix_fmt yuv420p` (even dimensions, 4:2:0) for H.264
+  encodes; the second form runs a caller filter chain first. `h264_compatible_filter(filters)` returns
+  the chain text. Written without compiling or running anything.
+- New (issue #581): `parse_time_duration(&str) -> Option<Duration>` reads the unsigned FFmpeg time
+  grammar (`HH:MM:SS[.m]`, `MM:SS`, seconds with a fraction, `90s`, `1500ms`, `250000us`) and refuses
+  signs, whitespace, exponents and overflow, so a caller can validate a model-supplied time and fill
+  `ExtractOptions::start`/`duration` (documented there). Written without compiling or running anything.
+- New (issue #739): `UnverifiedRequest::path_lookup(tool)` (a request that only searches `PATH` for the
+  bare `ffmpeg`/`ffprobe` name, development builds only) and `find_tool_on_path(tool)` (the location
+  alone, not catalog-checked). The existing `allow_path_lookup` field behaves as before.
+- Docs (issue #300): `quickprobe` states its coverage: duration, file size, codec (and audio codec)
+  and GIF frame count are probed; slide counts are not a media-container property and stay out.
+  Written without compiling or running anything.
+
 ## 0.2.10 (2026-10-18)
 
 - New (issue #479): "override first" for the one-call resolver. `ResolveOptions::new().override_first(path)`
